    "question": "Charley has a bag that contains 51 white beads and 90 black beads. He reaches in the bag and pulls out 1/6 of the black beads and a third of the white beads. How many beads in total did Charley pull out?",
    "gold": "32",
    "answer": "Charley pulled out 90/6 = <<90/6=15>>15 black beads.\nCharley pulled out 51/3 = <<51/3=17>>17 white beads.\nCharley pulled out 15+17 = <<15+17=32>>32 beads in total.\n#### 32"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many beads Charley pulled out, we need to calculate the number of black beads and white beads he pulled out separately and then sum them up.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the number of black beads Charley pulled out. The bag contains 90 black beads, and he pulls out \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) of them:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of black beads pulled out} = \\frac{1}{6} \\times 90 = 15\n\\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the number of white beads Charley pulled out. The bag contains 51 white beads, and he pulls out \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) of them:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of white beads pulled out} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 51 = 17\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the number of black beads and white beads Charley pulled out to find the total number of beads he pulled out:\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of beads pulled out} = 15 + 17 = 32\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of beads Charley pulled out is \\(\\boxed{32}\\).",
